# Backend: Logging + Audit Logs

## Application logs (pino)
- Use the shared pino instance (`backend/src/utils/logger.js`).
- Prefer structured logs: `logger.info({ requestId, userId, ... }, "message")`.
- Use request-scoped logger when available (`req.log`) and include `req.requestId`.

## Audit/business logs (logs table)
- Use `createLog(...)`.
- Do not store:
  - passwords
  - JWTs (access/refresh tokens)
  - Plaid access tokens
  - Cloudinary secrets
- Keep JSON fields small; truncate large blobs.

## Error logging
- Let the global error handler in `backend/src/app.js` handle responses.
- Log unexpected errors with context: `{ err, requestId, method, path, user }`.
